            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a pickpocket, then the Marathi for to cheat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: हवालदार",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हवालदार — havāldār — \"a constable\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आम्हाला किती वेळ थांबावं लागेल, हे हवालदारावर अवलंबून आहे. āmhālā kitī veḷ thāmbāvaṁ lāgel, he havāldārāvar avlambūn āhe. How long we will have to wait depends on the constable."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हवालदाराला, to the constable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हवालदार (havāldār) is a loan from Persian ḥavāladār, 'one entrusted with a charge', usually traced to Arabic ḥawāla, 'a charge, a trust'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
