        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अटक करणे",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अटक करणे — aṭak karṇe — \"to arrest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पोलिसांनी चोराला संध्याकाळी अटक केली. polisānnī corālā sandhyākāḷī aṭak kelī. The police arrested the thief in the evening."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with -ने (he …): त्याने अटक केली, tyāne aṭak kelī."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The person arrested takes -ला; अटक is feminine, so the past is अटक केली."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अटक करणे (aṭak karṇe) is built from aṭak, 'a hold, a stop', of the family CDIAL lists under aṭṭakk, 'obstruct, stop', with Marathi aṭakṇe, 'to be stopped' (CDIAL 182), and karṇe, 'to do'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
